+  "title": "AET-B-2: durable-effect record — a committed effect can be re-committed and replay reports one clean commit",
+  "problem": "🏛 **SARCHI** — **AET-B-2: the durable-effect record.** Rung B's second governed WP, gated on B-1 (#287 / PR #290) landing. Posting the spec measured rather than imagined: **most of this substrate already exists**, and the honest content of this rung is a three-item delta, one of which is a real hole.\n\n## Reuse first — what already exists, measured on `main`\n\nThe Lean ladder's first two questions answer themselves here. `run-ledger.jsonl` already implements the bulk of AET-I05:\n\n```\nhash-chained events, genesis + previous_event_hash        EXISTS\nall five contract resolutions in LEDGER_OUTCOMES          EXISTS\n  COMMITTED · PROVEN_ABSENT · OUTCOME_UNKNOWN · COMPENSATED · MANUAL_REMEDIATION\nTERMINAL_OUTCOMES correctly EXCLUDES OUTCOME_UNKNOWN      EXISTS\nreplay_run() — pure, re-executes nothing                  EXISTS\nplan_next_effect() — deny-unless-established              EXISTS\nappend_event() — verifies the chain before appending      EXISTS\n```\n\n**No new subsystem is warranted, and none is proposed.** A second effect-recording mechanism beside this one would be the \"no second gate\" failure at the substrate layer.\n\n## The delta — three gaps, all probed, with a positive control\n\n```\nPROBE 1  one effect: PREPARED -> COMMITTED -> PREPARED -> COMMITTED\n         ADMITTED (4 events). replay_run reports committed_effects=['EFF-1'],\n         unresolved=[] -- a durable external effect executed TWICE, and the\n         record reads as one clean commit.\nPROBE 2  an event carrying an undeclared key 'granted_authority': ADMITTED\n         (schemas/run-ledger-event.schema.json declares no additionalProperties)\nPROBE 3  positive control -- a bogus outcome 'TOTALLY_MADE_UP': REFUSED\n         (\"invalid outcome\") -- the instrument works, so 1 and 2 mean something\n```\n\n**Gap 1 is the rung's reason to exist.** `LEDGER_OUTCOMES` is a *membership* check at both consumers (the read path and the append path) — it is not a state machine. AET