discovered per schema.\n\n**Gap 3 is where the adversarial clause earns its keep.** A missing *witness* is invisible to any test that walks only the vocabulary that exists: every enum member can pass while the phase that was supposed to leave a trace left none. Criterion 6 is pointed here first.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. An effect whose last outcome is **terminal** cannot receive a further event: refused at `append_event` **and** at the ledger read path, with one semantic from **one authoritative site both consumers inherit** — not a guard per consumer (#290's whole lesson; validation at the source).\n2. The transition rule walks the **closed** set: every member of `LEDGER_OUTCOMES` is exercised as a predecessor, and the legal successors of each are asserted from the declared table rather than from the cases that happen to be convenient.\n3. `run-ledger-event.schema.json` declares `additionalProperties: false`; a probe carrying an undeclared key is refused, and the refusal is attributed to the walker (enforced) rather than assumed.\n4. The AUTHORITY CHECK phase is witnessed by the record: either a phase-bearing outcome term or a required field naming the authority consulted. Whichever is chosen, the **sole enforcer is stated in-line** (#264) and the choice is justified against the alternative in the PR body.\n5. Every new refusal is **red-first**, and each is mutation-killed with **per-consumer discrimination** where it has two consumers — a batch run proving \"at least one test reds\" does not prove inheritance.\n6. **Adversarial clause (#270, non-optional):** the criteria above certify the transitions we thought of. The battery additionally includes at least one sequence that is *not* in the declared table and *not* obviously illegal, and states which control refuses it or declares it non-covered. A criteria set that can only confirm the imagined fix is a plan defect, and this rung's subject — a record of things that already happened in the world — is where a silent gap costs the most.\n\n## Out of scope, stated\n\nNo executor, no runtime, no retry policy engine, no second ledger. This rung governs **the record**; the thing that performs effects is not built here and gains no authority from this landing. Compensation semantics (`COMPENSATED` → what, exactly) stay with the operation that owns them.\n\n## Tier and stage\n\nPatch — a bug fix plus test additions on an existing module; no new public surface. Change class C2. DEV Glossary stage: implementation of a frozen contract clause, no new vocabulary.\n\nGated on #290 landing. Ids claimed at bind time via the sweep, never here.\n\n<!-- agent: sarchi -->\n",
